<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Dutch Formosa</h1><p class="st-meta">1624 CE – 1662 CE · capital Fort Zeelandia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Dutch East India Company's colony in south-western Taiwan, which brought the first large-scale Chinese settlement to the island before Koxinga expelled it in 1662.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Seeking a base for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> trade, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dutch-east-india-company-territories">Dutch East India Company</a> failed to take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macau">Macau</a> in 1622 and occupied the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penghu">Penghu</a> islands, but a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming</a> fleet forced them out in 1624. By agreement they moved to Tayouan on the coast of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-china">Taiwan</a>, where they built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-zeelandia-taiwan">Fort Zeelandia</a>, within the sphere of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> territories in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Company ruled through a governor and council, subdued indigenous villages by force and treaty, and expelled the Spanish from the north in 1642. It recruited Chinese settlers to grow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a>, taxing them heavily, and exported deer skins to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. Reformed missionaries such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgius-candidius">Georgius Candidius</a> wrote the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siraya-people">Siraya</a> language in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> letters. Chinese discontent erupted in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guo-huaiyi-rebellion">Guo Huaiyi revolt</a> of 1652.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1661 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming</a> loyalist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koxinga">Koxinga</a> landed with a large fleet and besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-zeelandia-taiwan">Fort Zeelandia</a> for nine months. Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-coyett">Frederick Coyett</a> surrendered in February 1662, and the colony became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-tungning">Kingdom of Tungning</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/dutch-formosa.jpg" alt="Dutch Formosa" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Himasaram · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Dutch_East_India_Company.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1624 CE – 1662 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Fort Zeelandia</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Pieter Nuyts, Frederick Coyett</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Indigenous religions, Chinese folk religion, Reformed Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dutch, Siraya, Hokkien</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/taiwan">Taiwan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Formosa (Dutch)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1643&amp;focus=dutch-formosa" aria-label="Dutch Formosa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7890 1329 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Dutch Formosa lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8210 1585L5097 634M8210 1585L8210 1581M8210 1585L8228 1509"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5097 634h0M8210 1581h0M8228 1509h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8210 1585h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8210 1585h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Fort Zeelandia. <a href="/atlas?year=1643&amp;focus=dutch-formosa">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

